## what is left (t2t.open, 16 threads, after): entropy 0.35 s (rANS 31 %, axo_dna_decode bases 23 % of 1-thread CPU),
match 0.25 s (3.1 GB literals read + 3.1 GB written = 25 GB/s, ~60 % of the 42 GB/s traffic ceiling; does not scale
past 1 thread), first touch of fresh buffers. Next: write the literal stream straight into the output (no 3.1 GB
intermediate), SIMD base expansion in axo_dna_decode.
## default profile (zstd literals, what lzbench measures): libzstd 1.4.8 (system) vs 1.5.5 (static, asm Huffman, BMI2)
chr1 1 thread 0.184 -> 0.154 s, 8 threads 0.052 -> 0.050, 16 threads 0.065 -> 0.059; silesia 0.138 -> 0.138 / 0.040 -> 0.039
lzbench and TurboBench build their own zstd 1.5.x; the CLI on ace-core links the system 1.4.8 (make ZSTD_CFLAGS/ZSTD_LIBS to override).
